      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is a good idea. It\u0027s always been a hack in network monitor, but here you\u0027re making new system API of it so it\u0027s becoming worse.\n\nIf you look at UpstreamNetworkMonitor#startTrackDefaultNetwork it has another hacky way of doing this which is less invasive, and I suggest you convert to that method. If you\u0027re moving Tethering into the network stack app you might even be able to unify these two things. That hack is bad too and has drawbacks over your current design, but overall I favor it for not needing this system API (especially if you manage to unify it with UNM, but I doubt you will).\n\nIf you can\u0027t use this scheme for some reason, I want to point out that NetworkMonitor is not even using this request you\u0027re sending here, but only the capabilities inside it, which I think never change (and if I\u0027m wrong and they do, you are not sending the changes over in this patchset anyway). Sending only the capabilities would be a well needed reduction of surface.\n\nEventually it\u0027s probably a good idea to have some true and nice system API that will let the NETWORK_STACK holding apps about the default system network without need for hacks. But this is not it, and I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a good idea to do it now.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2045,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 2045,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "f5b761d33701d84a708915aed5e570d711a51402",
